
OPTIMIZATIONS

Optimizations are carried out for the molecule in the acmphn.z file
(acetaminophen) 

Execute via
xOPT acmphn           - this is for an optimization with OPLS-AA
xOPTFGB acmphn        - this is an optimization using OPLS-AA with GB/SA solvation
xAM1OPT acmphn        - this is for an optimization with AM1    
xPDGOPT acmphn        - this is for an optimization with PDDG/PM3

Each job writes the output to out (printed output) and plt.pdb
(PDB file of structure). So, the second job will write over the files
from the first one unless you rename them. The file sum contains the
resultant optimized Z-matrix.

To display the output plt.pdb file, enter
xRAS

Time required for full optimization of acetaminophen:
with OPLS-AA on a 2.4 GHz Pentium:     2 sec for BFGS optimization
with AM1 or PDG on a 2.4 GHz Pentium: 15 sec for Fletcher-Powell optimization

The files OPLSout, GBout, AM1out, and PDGout contain 
the full output as executed by W. Jorgensen.
_______________________________________________________________________________

The same input Z-matrix was used in these two cases; however, the Z-matrix
file could be simplified for the quantum calculations
since the OPLS-AA atom types and specification of additional parameters and
dihedral types are not needed. The atomic numbers are given instead of the
OPLS-AA atom types. If the OPLS-AA atom types are given, there is  no
problem as BOSS looks up the atomic numbers in the oplsaa.par file.
The acmphnQM.z file illustrates the simplifications - compare it with acmphn.z.
xPDGOPT acmphnQM
