OPTIMIZATION of a COMPLEX
benwpi.z contains the Z-matrix for the benzene-water (TIP4P) complex.
Display the Z-matrix; note the use of TERZ to separate the two molecules
and the treatment of the TIP4P water molecule with the rigid geometry
and 4th site for the partial negative charge. Optimize via
xOPTF benwpi  [xOPTF (Fletcher-Powell)  and  xOPT (BFGS) both work well -  
               sometimes it is worth checking more than one optimizer;
               also watch for optimization to a saddle-point rather than 
               a minimum.]
Total energy = 2.89 kcal/mol
To compute the interaction energy, the optimized energy for benzene is needed.
xOPTF benzen
Total energy = 6.68 kcal/mol
Energy of TIP4P water = 0 since it is rigid.
benzene + TIP4P water -> benzene...water
deltaE = 2.89 - 6.68 - 0 = -3.79 kcal/mol
