SINGLE-POINT QM CALCULATIONS for CHARGES
One can obtain the CM1 charges and Lennard-Jones parameters
for the solute(s) by doing a single-point AM1 or PM3 calculation.
Use the scripts:
xAM1SP acmphnQM 
xPM3SP acmphnQM 
The resultant charges and Lennard-Jones parameters are written
to the sum file along with the Z-matrix modified to use the atom-type
numbers (800-899) assigned for the new parameters. One could then replace
the original Z-matrix with this one.

For CM3 charges, use the xAM1CM3, xPM3CM3 and xPDGCM3 scripts.

OPLS/CM1A FORCE FIELD (PNAS 102, 6665 (2005) - in boss/bossman) 
To obtain converged CM1A charges, one should perform a series of
xAM1SP and xOPT cycles. This is done with the script xZCM1A - use
it to get converged 1.14*CM1A charges for neutral molecules,e.g.,
xZCM1A benzen
The optimized OPLS/CM1A Z-matrix is in the output sum file.

For a cation, use xZCM1A+  
For an anion, use xZCM1A-  
